      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the delete path use exact per-FIB/per-AF lookups instead of the default-policy fallback? A delete for a FIB with no explicit policy currently resolves to and frees the default policy. Likewise, for an IPv6-only FIB policy, the IPv4 lookup falls back to default and is selected before the FIB’s IPv6 entry. Please reject deletes where neither family has an explicit entry; when only one family is configured, delete that explicit entry rather than the default fallback.",
